From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 21:20:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] winewayland: Restore compositor-maximized windows that can't be maximized.

Windows can't maximize a window without a maximize box or a sizing frame,
and such windows only draw at their own size. winewayland sets their
minimum and maximum size to their size, but some compositors maximize new
windows anyway: with Umbriel's default_maximize, the Guild Wars 2 launcher
(WS_POPUP | WS_MINIMIZEBOX) got WS_MAXIMIZE and a screen-sized window it
never drew into, and only appeared once it was moved (#1007).

Unless the application maximized the window itself, treat such a
configure as an unmaximized one without a size, so the window keeps its
size, and ask the compositor to restore it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff -ruN a/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c b/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
@@ -1134,6 +1134,25 @@
     surface->processing = surface->requested;
     memset(&surface->requested, 0, sizeof(surface->requested));
 
+    /* Windows can't maximize a window without a maximize box or a sizing
+     * frame, and such windows only draw at their own size. Some compositors
+     * maximize new windows anyway (Umbriel's default_maximize), even though
+     * we set their minimum and maximum size to their size: the Guild Wars 2
+     * launcher then became a blank screen-sized window. Unless the
+     * application maximized the window itself, keep its size and ask the
+     * compositor to restore it. */
+    style = NtUserGetWindowLongW(hwnd, GWL_STYLE);
+    if ((surface->processing.state & WAYLAND_SURFACE_CONFIG_STATE_MAXIMIZED) &&
+        !(surface->processing.state & WAYLAND_SURFACE_CONFIG_STATE_FULLSCREEN) &&
+        !(style & (WS_MAXIMIZEBOX | WS_THICKFRAME | WS_MAXIMIZE | WS_CHILD)) &&
+        surface->xdg_toplevel)
+    {
+        TRACE("hwnd=%p can't be maximized, asking the compositor to restore it\n", hwnd);
+        surface->processing.state &= ~WAYLAND_SURFACE_CONFIG_STATE_MAXIMIZED;
+        SetRectEmpty(&surface->processing.rect);
+        xdg_toplevel_unset_maximized(surface->xdg_toplevel);
+    }
+
     state = surface->processing.state;
     /* Ignore size hints if we don't have a state that requires strict
      * size adherence, in order to avoid spurious resizes.
